1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
And now it's the old scout master,

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:09,000
The old scouter.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
He likes to come and visit the troop meetings once in a while.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
He likes to keep up with what we're doing and you know, talk scouting.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
He's getting on in years. so his wife has to help him get there.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,000
She drives him over to the meeting house and helps him get inside

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
and she'll sit there with him and it's great.

8
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,000
He can talk to the scouts and share stories and things like that.

9
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,000
and he was there the other night and I said:

10
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
listen, do you remember? you told me about a backpacking trail

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000
You used to take the scouts out on and it had a waterfall.

12
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:44,000
It was a beautiful place and I can't remember the name of the place.

13
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Do you remember the name of the place?

14
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,000
He says, oh, of course. of course I remember the name.

15
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
And I said: well, can you tell me what it was?

16
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,000
He says, oh, yeah, yeah,

17
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,000
What's the name of the flower?

18
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,000
The red flower, right,

19
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Did she get for Valentine's Day?

20
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,000
And stuff like that.

21
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
I said: do you mean Rose?

22
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,000
And he says that's right, that's right.

23
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,000
And he turns to his wife and he says: Rose,

24
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:11,000
what was the name of the trail with the waterfall where I used to

25
